BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      # The Myth of the River of Plenty) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of the magical River of Plenty. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (         river had a wondrous property: any gift cast into its waters would emerge on the far sh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        ore tripled in abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      The Elder of the First Village possessed five loaves of bread each moon. She could choose ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        to keep all five, or cast some into the river for the Second Village. Whatever arrived-f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        ifteen times what she sent-belonged to the Second Village's Elder, who then decided what) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (         to send back across the waters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      At first, fear ruled both shores. "What if I give and receive nothing?" worried the First ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        Elder. "What if they expect too much in return?" fretted the Second Elder.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      But one wise woman said: "The river multiplies gifts, not because it demands perfection, b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        ut because it rewards the courage to begin. Send with open hands, return with grateful h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        earts, and both villages shall flourish.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      When both Elders embraced this wisdom-giving generously and returning fairly-the River of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        Plenty flowed abundantly. The villages learned that trust, once begun, creates more than) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (         either could hoard alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
