BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      But the Second Guardian's response was silence. No acorns came.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      The First Guardian waited at the well's edge, searching for meaning. Was this the storm's ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        noise speaking once more, garbling the exchange? Was this a test-"prove your faith means) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (         something when nothing flows back"? Or had the Second Guardian simply chosen to hoard t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        heir five, trusting no longer?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      The ritual demanded response. The well had given the First Guardian nothing, so nothing co) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        uld be returned. Not as punishment, not as revenge-simply as reality. Empty hands cannot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (         give.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      The ancient stones seemed to weep. The cycle that had once flourished-trust met with trust) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        , abundance shared freely-now lay fractured. Both Guardians had been wounded by fog and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        confusion. Both had reached toward restoration at different moments, ships passing in th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        e mist.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      The First Guardian carved words into stone: "When the well runs dry, even willing hearts c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        annot give. The cycle cannot be rebuilt by one alone. Both must risk again, must send ag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        ain, must believe the other remembers what we once were.") Tj ET
